\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {20}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Allometric body-size scaling of the pelvic eigenvalue spectrum.} \textbf  {(A)}~Scaling exponents $\beta _{\rm  scale}$ per mode from IV-2SLS regression of $\log \lambda $ on $\log s$ (isotropic scale); bars = point estimate, whiskers = 95\,\% CI, stars = FDR$<$0.05, dashed line = classical $\lambda \propto L^{-2}$. \textbf  {(B)}~Shapley/LMG $R^2$ decomposition: share of eigenvalue variance explained by scale (purple), sex (teal), shape (orange), and material (blue). \textbf  {(C)}~Mode 9--10 swap probability vs.\ isotropic scale, sex-stratified; curve = logistic fit. \textbf  {(D)}~Relative spectral gap$_{\rm  in}$(9--10) vs.\ scale with LOWESS trend; sex coded by color/marker. \textbf  {(E)}~SIJ rotation magnitude across LAB phases vs.\ body size. \textbf  {(F)}~Energy-fraction sensitivity (pp per IQR of log-scale) across five load cases.}}{49}{figure.20}\protected@file@percent }
